 "scenes": [
  {
   "id": "intro",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Everything so far issued one instruction per cycle, so the best CPI was 1. To beat that, issue several per cycle. Combine that with Tomasulo and speculation, and you have the core of every modern laptop and phone processor."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "head"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Multiple issue with dynamic scheduling"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Here are the seven stages."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "stages"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The kinds of multiple issue, what makes it hard, and one loop run on a 2-issue machine without speculation."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "stages[0..=2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Then the same loop with speculation, a comparison, the VLIW alternative, and an exam question."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "stages[3..=6]"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "kinds",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 1: Module 1 introduced superscalar and VLIW machines. Here is where they sit now."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 1 of 7: several per cycle"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "stages"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "kinds"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A statically scheduled superscalar issues a few instructions per cycle, in order. Simple, but one stall stops everything."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "kinds[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A VLIW lets the compiler pack independent operations into one long instruction. We return to it at the end."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "kinds[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A dynamically scheduled superscalar issues several per cycle into Tomasulo-style stations, with a reorder buffer and speculation. Every high-performance core today works this way."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "kinds[2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "today: wide issue + out of order + speculation"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "hard",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 2: the hard part is issue itself. In one cycle, the issue stage must handle a whole group of instructions."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 2 of 7: what makes it hard"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "kinds"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "hard"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Find a free station and a free ROB entry for each of them."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "hard[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Check whether any instruction in the group needs the result of an earlier one in the same group. Each source must be compared with every earlier destination."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "hard[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "With w instructions of two sources each, that is w times w minus 1 comparisons. 2 for a 2-wide machine, 12 for 4-wide, 56 for 8-wide. Every cycle."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "hm"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "hm[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "And the register map must be updated for the whole group in order, so the last writer in the group wins. This logic is one reason issue widths have stayed between about 4 and 8."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "hard[2]"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "nospec",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 3: an integer loop that adds 1 to every array element."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 3 of 7: 2-issue, no speculation"
