      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "tn[1]",
       "delay": 0.4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The branch depends on the add's R2, so it executes in 7."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "tn[4]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Now the second iteration's load. It issued back in cycle 3, and its address R1 was ready in 4. But it is behind a branch, so it may not start until cycle 8."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "tn[5]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "tn[4][3]",
       "delay": 0.4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Every iteration waits for the previous branch. The branches commit in 9, 15, and 21: 6 cycles per iteration, though the machine could issue an iteration every 2.5."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "tn[9]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "tn[4][5]",
       "delay": 0.4
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "no speculation: each iteration waits for the last branch"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "spec",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 4: the same loop, with speculation. The branch is predicted taken, and later instructions may execute before it resolves."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 4 of 7: with speculation"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "tn"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "ts"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Iteration 1 is unchanged: the load, the add, the store, the branch."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "ts[0..=4]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "But iteration 2's load starts in cycle 5, as soon as R1 is ready, instead of 8. Its add, store and branch follow 3 cycles behind iteration 1."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "ts[5]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "ts[6..=9]",
       "delay": 0.4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Results finish out of order, but commit still marches in order, 2 per cycle. The branches commit in 9, 12 and 15."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "ts[4][5]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "ts[9][5]",
       "delay": 0.4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "If a prediction had been wrong, the ROB would flush the work behind it, exactly as in the last video. Here every iteration but the last guesses right."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "speculation: the next iteration runs before the branch is known"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "cmp",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 5: side by side."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 5 of 7: comparing"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "ts"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "cm"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Without speculation, an iteration every 6 cycles. With it, every 3. Twice as fast, on the same hardware."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "cm[0..=1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "In instructions per cycle: 0.83 against 1.67. Speculation is what lets a wide machine actually use its width."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "cm[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Can it go faster still? Each iteration has 5 instructions, and only 2 issue per cycle, so an iteration needs at least 2.5 cycles to issue. Run ten iterations and the speculative machine settles close to that limit. The non-speculative one stays at 6."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "cm[1][2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "cm[2][2]",
       "delay": 0.5
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "And issue is not the only thing that must widen."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "cm"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "lim"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Fetch must deliver several instructions per cycle, and predict a branch among them. There must be enough result buses and register ports for several results per cycle."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "lim[0..=1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Commit must keep up, or finished instructions pile up in the ROB. And the ROB and stations must be big enough to hold the instructions in flight."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "lim[2..=3]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "issue, buses, commit and ROB must all widen together"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "vliw",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 6: the static alternative. A VLIW instruction is a packet with fixed slots, for example 2 memory operations, 2 floating-point operations, and 1 integer or branch."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 6 of 7: VLIW"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "lim"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "vliw"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "vliw[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The compiler fills the slots, mostly by unrolling loops. The hardware performs no dependence checks at all, so it is simple and low power."
     },
     "do": [
